<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zayyanid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Zayyanid, Zayyanids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zayyanid dynasty was a Berber dynasty that ruled the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, from the thirteenth to the sixteenth century. Of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zanata-berbers">Zanata</a> origin, it emerged from the fragmentation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a>. The Zayyanid seizure of Tlemcen around 1236 carved the central Maghreb out of the Almohad domain.</p></div>
